Title: The transcript archive copies every root the context audit reads
Created: 2026-11-10
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-11-10T13:34Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 1519 makes `scripts/trace-compact-audit.py` read the other hosts from
the transcript archive. The author then ruled, on 2026-11-10: "Then ensure
archives covers all surfaces." The archive's roots are defined in
`scripts/transcript_spool.py` (`live_roots`, `source_roots`, the spool); the
audit's readers define theirs again (`read_codex` walks `sessions/` and
`archived_sessions/` under the Codex home; `default_pi_sessions`,
`default_pi_spool`). Two definitions drift.

Counted on 2026-11-10 (paths and counts only):

- padme, files older than a day against archived files: Claude Code 24309
  eligible, 27610 archived (the archive keeps sessions since deleted); Codex
  `sessions/` 3504 against 3503; Pi 78 live and 28 spool against 106 (78
  nested, 28 flat); aider 4 against 4; vibe 78 against 78.
- doudou: Codex 1335 against 1335; Pi 48 against 48; Claude Code 23406
  eligible, 26873 archived; no spool directory. padme's copy of `raw/doudou`
  has the same counts as doudou's own, runtime by runtime.
- `~/.codex/archived_sessions` is not a source root: `source_roots('codex')`
  is `sessions/` only. padme has 19 rollouts there, 18 of them in
  `raw/padme/codex` by file name (copied while still under `sessions/`), 1 in
  no copy; doudou has 11.
- Pi live sessions and the Pi spool are both copied under `raw/<host>/pi`.
  The audit holds a live session to its model's ceiling and a spool session
  to the default; in the archive the two are told apart only by depth.

## Scope

- Each runtime's roots have one definition, in `scripts/transcript_spool.py`,
  used by the archive and by the audit's readers: a root the audit reads is
  by construction a root the archive copies.
- `archived_sessions/` under the Codex home becomes a source root of the
  archive. A rollout copied earlier from `sessions/` and again from
  `archived_sessions/` is one session to any reader of the archive.
- The archive's own code says, for an archived file, which source root it
  came from (Pi live or Pi spool, Codex sessions or archived sessions). No
  existing archived file moves or is rewritten.

Out of scope: the archive's layout, schedule and push; readers for aider and
vibe in the audit; this host's sessions already deleted from the live trees.

Note for whoever lands it: the nightly run on each host uses that host's
checkout, so the other host copies `archived_sessions/` from its first
nightly run after it syncs.

## Test

On temporary roots: a rollout under `archived_sessions/` is archived; the
same rollout present under both Codex directories resolves to one session;
an archived Pi spool file and an archived Pi live file are each attributed to
their source root; a runtime root added to the one definition is walked by
the archive and offered to the audit without a second edit.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A rollout under `~/.codex/archived_sessions` is copied by the archive
  run, and counts once however many copies the archive holds
- [ ] Every root the audit reads for a runtime comes from the one definition
  in `scripts/transcript_spool.py` that the archive walks
- [ ] For an archived file, the archive's code names its source root; no
  existing archived file moves
- [ ] `make check` passes
